# Backend (`apps/backend`)

Hono API on Node (`@hono/node-server`). Auth: **Better Auth**.

## Application boundaries

Current directory names and file shapes are conventions to inspect, not a fixed
template. For a structural change or an overloaded unit, load
`repository-structure` and preserve the boundaries below.

- Application assembly, global middleware, and auth setup do not own domain
  workflows. Connect capability endpoints through the existing routing
  composition boundary.
- HTTP handlers are transport delivery: validate structured input, call the
  appropriate domain capability, then return the HTTP response.
- Domain behavior does not depend on Hono `Context` or response helpers.
- Technical adapters (environment, Redis, queues, logging, auth, errors) do not
  import domain modules.

## Core rules

| Rule               | Detail                                                                                                                                           |
| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| No RoR controllers | Use Hono handlers; prefer path inference                                                                                                          |
| Auth               | Better Auth at `/api/auth/*` via `auth.handler`; do not reimplement login/register                                                               |
| Admin auth         | Any `/api/admin/**` route must use `requireAdmin`; hiding navigation or relying on web proxy is not authorization                                |
| Validation         | Validate structured request data with Zod (`@hono/zod-validator` or shared schemas). Multipart or stream boundaries may validate transport constraints locally before domain code runs |
| Errors             | Self-owned Hono APIs return `{ error, details? }`. Prefer `sendError` / `sendValidationError` from `src/lib/response.ts` for reusable or middleware paths; a boundary-local response is allowed when it keeps that contract |

Better Auth native `/api/auth/*` responses are allowed to keep Better Auth's contract; do not wrap or normalize those endpoints locally.

## Env

`getEnvConfig()` in `src/lib/env.ts` loads package `.env` and Zod-`parse`s it (fail fast at import/boot). Call sites read the exported `env` object — no `process.env` scattered in modules, no one-off getters per variable. Keep only vars the runtime actually reads.

A narrow boundary adapter may read conventional platform variables directly when
it must preserve inherited runtime behavior (for example, standard proxy
variables); do not spread that exception into application or domain code.
